{% extends "base.html.j2" %}
{% import "macros.html.j2" as m %}
{% block title %}Rules{% endblock %}
{% block toc %}
{{ m.toc_item("p-hard", "Hard limits", "code") }}
{{ m.toc_item("p-core", "Core rules", "risk") }}
{% if book.swing %}{{ m.toc_item("p-swing", "Swing rules", "scout") }}{% endif %}
{% endblock %}
{% block hero %}
<header class="hero">
  <p class="eyebrow">Rules</p>
  <h1>The rules the council works inside</h1>
  <p class="lede">Code enforces every rule; the prompts only explain them. The council cannot change any number here except one: the swing budget, which it votes on each run inside a range code clamps. Any other change is a policy change, recorded in every sealed run by the policy file's hash.</p>
</header>
{% endblock %}
{% macro card(r) %}
<article class="rule-card accent-{{ r.seat }}" id="{{ r.id }}" aria-labelledby="{{ r.id }}-h">
  <h3 class="rule-h" id="{{ r.id }}-h"><span class="rule-badge rb-{{ r.seat }}">{{ r.badge if r.badge is defined else r.id }}</span> {{ r.title }}</h3>
  <p class="rule-plain">{{ r.plain }}</p>
  {% if r.numbers %}
  <details class="jd accent-{{ r.seat }} rule-more">
    <summary><strong>Show the numbers</strong> <span class="jd-sum">{{ plural(r.numbers | length, "value") }}</span></summary>
    <div class="jd-body">
      <dl class="rule-nums">{% for k, v in r.numbers %}<div><dt>{{ k }}</dt><dd class="n">{{ v }}</dd></div>{% endfor %}</dl>
    </div>
  </details>
  {% endif %}
  {% if r.codes %}
  <p class="rule-codes small"><span class="jd-k">Reason codes it can give</span>{% for c in r.codes %}<span class="rule-code"><code class="jc-code">{{ r.id }}:{{ c.code }}</code> {{ c.words }}</span>{% endfor %}</p>
  {% endif %}
</article>
{% endmacro %}
{% block main %}

{% call m.section("p-hard", 1, "Hard limits", "code") %}
<p>Constants in the code. The policy files may be stricter, never looser, and a test enforces it.</p>
<div class="rule-grid">{% for r in book.hard %}{{ card(r) }}{% endfor %}</div>
{% endcall %}

{% call m.section("p-core", 2, "Core rules", "risk") %}
<p>Every rule the risk engine checks on every run of the core council. Shares are of the portfolio's value; a line's "full size" is the weight the rules alone would give it.</p>
<div class="rule-grid">{% for r in book.core %}{{ card(r) }}{% endfor %}</div>
<p class="muted small">Source: <code>policy/risk.yaml</code>. Its hash is recorded in every sealed run.</p>
{% endcall %}

{% if book.swing %}
{% call m.section("p-swing", 3, "Swing rules", "scout") %}
<p>The swing book's rules, run twice: on each idea before the Skeptic sees it, and on the manager's entries before a paper leg is built. Exits are never refused. The <span class="rule-badge rb-skeptic">S11</span> badge marks the rule that also sets the Skeptic's starting lean.</p>
<div class="rule-grid">{% for r in book.swing %}{{ card(r) }}{% endfor %}</div>
<p class="muted small">Source: <code>policy/swing.yaml</code>. Nothing here trades with money while the swing book's go-live switch is off.</p>
{% endcall %}
{% endif %}
{% endblock %}
